# Cross-origin isolation for the wasm edit-host (Phase 5). The Web Worker drives its
# run loop off a SharedArrayBuffer (slice 5d), which the browser only exposes when the
# document is cross-origin isolated. These three headers make `crossOriginIsolated`
# true; without them the page falls back to the slower postMessage transport and timers
# (vim.defer_fn / nx.timer) never fire.
#
# This is the Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_headers` format — drop `web/` (this dir) and
# the built `dist/` alongside it as the publish root. For nginx / Apache / other hosts,
# set the same three headers on every response (see README → "Serving in production").
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# The `nx.http.mount` Service Worker (nx-sw.js), which serves a plugin's mounted subroutes
# at /plugin/*. It is served from this root, but a Service Worker's scope defaults to its
# own directory — `Service-Worker-Allowed` is what lets it register with scope "/" so it can
# see /plugin/* at all. Without this the registration is REJECTED and every mount 404s.
# `no-cache` because a stale worker would serve a mount contract the editor no longer speaks.
/nx-sw.js
  Service-Worker-Allowed: /
  Cache-Control: no-cache
